{"explanation": "The most reliable signal is subject size. The unit is clearly more active when the main subject fills a quarter or more of the frame than when it is small or distant (rows 7 and 8, d about +1.0). It is somewhat more active when the subject is cut off by the frame edge, which fits the same close-up preference. This size preference is partly shared with similar units 2 and 3, so it is not unique to this unit. The apparent colour-tint effects did not hold up. The warm-over-neutral tint effect reversed on new photos (row 18, d -0.27). The black-and-white comparisons rested on only 5 colourless photos and could not be checked on the new set, so a colour or tint preference is not established.", "rows": [7, 8]}
```

